@lang en
IMPORT prelude
IMPORT domain

-- g7-electrical.l4: sections 58 and 61 of the Regulation of Engagement in Work on Refrigeration or
-- Air-Conditioning Systems Law 5785-2025: what the Law does to the licensee's position under the Electricity Law.
--
-- Written by ENCODER G7.  Imports only `prelude` and `domain`.
--
-- Section 58 deems a licensee to hold a service-electrician licence for cooling systems.  It is encoded as a
-- decision.  Section 61 amends the Electricity Law (adds subsection (e) to its section 6); the amended statute is
-- OUT OF SCOPE (the brief), so what section 61 decides enters as three input facts and the rule below only states,
-- in the words of the added subsection, when they entitle a licensee to do electrical work.  The Electricity Law's
-- own section 6(a), which "without derogating from" the added subsection still stands, is not modelled.
--
-- Inputs from other groups, under their standard names (PLAN section (c)):
--   IP1  `licence kinds in force on the day`   the kinds of licence the person holds in force on the day asked
--                                               about (decided by G2 and G1; an empty list means none)
--   IP4  `the act is work on a cooling system` whether the act is "work on a cooling system" under section 2 and
--                                               the First Schedule (decided by G1)
--   and, for section 61, `the electrical work is in accordance with the First Schedule` (G1's items A12 and B14:
--   only the "integral" electrical system).
-- Not gated on commencement: section 63(a) fixes a commencement only "for the performance of work", and a licence
-- cannot be in force before the Law's licensing provisions operate, so the licence list already carries it (trap
-- T20; fork F-E-2 in FRAGMENT-G7.md).

§ `Chapter 7 — Miscellaneous provisions: electrical work (sections 58 and 61)`

§§ `58. Electrical work`

-- src:436 | {{ח:סעיף|58|ביצוע עבודות חשמל}}
-- src:437 | {{ח:ת}} יראו בעל רישיון לבצע עבודה במערכת קירור או מיזוג אוויר מכוח חוק זה כבעל רישיון חשמלאי–שירות לעניין מערכות קירור או מיזוג אוויר לפי {{ח:חיצוני|חוק החשמל#סעיף 6|סעיף 6 לחוק החשמל}}; אין באמור כדי לגרוע מהוראות כל דין, ובכלל זה הוראות {{ח:חיצוני|חוק החשמל|חוק החשמל}}.
@ref s.58 (src:436-437)
@export Whether a holder of a licence under the Israeli Law on work on refrigeration and air-conditioning systems is, for work on cooling systems, treated as holding a service-electrician licence under section 6 of the Electricity Law (section 58)
GIVEN `licence kinds in force on the day` IS A LIST OF `Licence kind` @desc The kinds of licence (grade 1, 2 or 3) that the person holds and that are in force on the day asked about; an empty list if none
      `the act is work on a cooling system` IS A BOOLEAN @desc True if the act is work on a cooling system under section 2 and the First Schedule of the Law
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the licensee is treated as a service electrician under section 58` `licence kinds in force on the day` `the act is work on a cooling system` MEANS
        NOT null `licence kinds in force on the day`
    AND `the act is work on a cooling system`

-- The second limb of section 58, "nothing in this is to derogate from the provisions of any law, including the
-- Electricity Law", is a saving: it keeps whatever other law requires.  It gates no decision and computes no value
-- here, so it is carried as inert text; which way the omission errs: it can only make the deeming above look
-- wider than it is, because the deeming holds "for cooling systems" and subject to every other requirement of law.
@ref s.58 (src:437)
`s 58 — the saving of other law` MEANS
    "Summary, not a quotation (the Hebrew above governs): the deeming of a licensee as a service electrician does not derogate from the provisions of any law, including the Electricity Law."

§§ `61. Amendment of the Electricity Law (No. 7)`

-- The wiki says only that the text was incorporated into the Electricity Law (the two lines quoted here).  The
-- gazette prints the added subsection on printed page 197 (page image viewed; the text layer is scrambled and is not
-- quoted).  In words (my translation of the page image, not a quotation): in section 6 of the Electricity Law,
-- 5714-1954, add at the end subsection (e): without derogating from subsection (a), a person may engage in
-- electrical work in accordance with the First Schedule of the Regulation of Engagement in Work on Refrigeration
-- or Air-Conditioning Systems Law, 5785-2025, within work on a refrigeration or air-conditioning system, if he
-- holds a licence to perform work on a refrigeration or air-conditioning system under that Law.
-- DISPOSITION: out-of-scope as a statute (the Electricity Law); its effect is carried here by the rule below, which
-- reads three input facts and nothing of the Electricity Law's own text.
-- src:453 | {{ח:סעיף|61|}}
-- src:454 | {{ח:ת}} {{ח:הערה|הנוסח שולב {{ח:חיצוני|חוק החשמל|בחוק החשמל, התשי״ד–1954}}.}}
@ref s.61 (src:453-454); gazette printed page 197
GIVEN `licence kinds in force on the day` IS A LIST OF `Licence kind` @desc The kinds of licence that the person holds and that are in force on the day asked about; an empty list if none
      `the act is work on a cooling system` IS A BOOLEAN @desc True if the electrical work is done within work on a cooling system
      `the electrical work is in accordance with the First Schedule` IS A BOOLEAN @desc True if the electrical work is of a kind the First Schedule lists (items A12 and B14 reach only the integral electrical system)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 61 — the licensee may do electrical work under subsection (e) added to section 6 of the Electricity Law` `licence kinds in force on the day` `the act is work on a cooling system` `the electrical work is in accordance with the First Schedule` MEANS
        `the electrical work is in accordance with the First Schedule`
    AND `the act is work on a cooling system`
    AND NOT null `licence kinds in force on the day`

§§ `58 against 61: two provisions that open electrical work to the licensee on different terms (fork F-E-1)`

-- Section 58 makes the licensee a service electrician for cooling systems, with no limit drawn from the First
-- Schedule.  Section 61 lets the licensee do electrical work only "in accordance with the First Schedule".  The Law does not
-- say which of the two governs electrical work on a cooling system that the First Schedule does not list.
-- The two readings are the two functions below; neither is the answer of the Law.
@ref s.58 (src:436-437); s.61 (src:453-454)
GIVEN `licence kinds in force on the day` IS A LIST OF `Licence kind`
      `the act is work on a cooling system` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`electrical work is open to the licensee, reading section 58 as a wide gateway` `licence kinds in force on the day` `the act is work on a cooling system` MEANS
    `the licensee is treated as a service electrician under section 58` `licence kinds in force on the day` `the act is work on a cooling system`

@ref s.58 (src:436-437); s.61 (src:453-454)
GIVEN `licence kinds in force on the day` IS A LIST OF `Licence kind`
      `the act is work on a cooling system` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the electrical work is in accordance with the First Schedule` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`electrical work is open to the licensee, reading section 61 as the only gateway` `licence kinds in force on the day` `the act is work on a cooling system` `the electrical work is in accordance with the First Schedule` MEANS
    `s 61 — the licensee may do electrical work under subsection (e) added to section 6 of the Electricity Law` `licence kinds in force on the day` `the act is work on a cooling system` `the electrical work is in accordance with the First Schedule`
